<title>USA: USDA to name new Farm Service Agency chief Friday.</title>
<headline>USDA to name new Farm Service Agency chief Friday.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday it will name the new chief of the Farm Service Agency (FSA) on Friday.</p>
<p>FSA runs federal farm subsidies, crop insurance, the Conservation Reserve, and farm ownership and operating loan programs. The agency has nearly 20,000 workers at offices across the country.</p>
<p>USDA said Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman will hold a news conference at 1000 EDT/1400 GMT to announce the appointment.</p>
<p>Grant Buntrock, the previous FSA administrator, resigned in April.</p>
